lib/IO/K8s/AutoGen.pm:348-351 -- after karr #57 fixed boolean array items,
two item types still fall into the [ Str ] default:

  items: { type: "object" }   --> ArrayRef[Str], rejects the hashrefs
  items: { type: "array"  }   --> ArrayRef[Str], rejects the arrayrefs

Same failure shape as #57: schema-conforming data dies on a type
constraint that never names the real problem (a wrongly generated
attribute type).

Unlike #57 this is NOT an AutoGen-only fix. The k8s DSL has no
array-of-hash and no array-of-array form -- inside an arrayref it accepts
only Str, Int, Bool and class names. So AutoGen has nothing correct to
map these onto; the work is a DSL + registry + serializer change in
lib/IO/K8s/Resource.pm first, then the AutoGen mapping.

Related: karr #63 wants a hash-of-scalar-type form in the same DSL. If
both are done, do them as one DSL extension rather than two.

